kobrakai's third season is full of  tension and surprises  kris takes over cobra kai with no mercy  daniel and johnny team up  and all three sensei confront their  pasts as they prepare to settle their  present-day differences  let's break down the explosive ending  and what it may mean for season four  after robbie makes miyagido infamous for  what happened during the school  melee in season two daniel finds that  his karate themed advertisements  aren't so cute anymore as his car sales  begin to drag  his top competitor tom cole secures an  exclusive distribution deal with doyona  and offers to buy daniel's dealership at  a bargain price  but daniel decides to take a trip to  japan instead  after an inauspicious meeting with  toyona daniel visits mr miyagi's home  in okinawa and reunites with kumiko the  young woman he defended  and had a romantic relationship with in  the karate kid part 2.  kumako has several surprises in store  for daniel  at tomi village including mr miyagi's  old love letters to her late aunt yuki  and a visit from the now grown woman he  rescued from a typhoon as a child  she's now vp of international sales at  doyona and as a long overdue reward for  saving her life so many years before  she steps in to save his business  relationship with the company  not only does the larusso auto group  come out of their pr nightmare  relatively  unscathed in the end but they also  convince anush to return to their team  and find that cousin louis is actually a  pretty solid salesman  with the dealership on solid ground once  again daniel will be able to focus on  his more personal matters going forward  another familiar face kumiko brings back  into the picture  is that of chosen who daniel defeated in  a brutal fight in the karate kid part 2.  rather than holding a grudge however  chozen wants to make amends  chozen reveals that his sensei sato was  also trained by miyagi's teacher  so he has inherited several artifacts  from miyagi's dojo and wants to test  whether miyagi really taught daniel  everything he knew  during a match chosen stuns daniel by  striking several pressure points and  disabling his limbs  a maneuver he attributes to miyagi's  teachings after pinning daniel  chosin ends the fight by honking his  nose which is a playful nod to how  daniel ended their vicious bout  so many years before chosen admits he  has felt shame for his behavior back  then  and is relieved to learn that daniel has  forgiven him in return  chosen agrees to train daniel and  miyagi's powerful move  and also gives him a cherished scroll  from miyagi's collection to take home  not only does daniel walk away with a  newfound peace agreement with chosen  he's also armed with a very effective  new defense technique  [Music]  only every rival we can end like this in  addition to saving his business  and learning a new trick in japan daniel  also gets some closure with kumako  though the two had an intense connection  in okinawa all those decades ago  they lost touch with one another and  moved on with their lives  the two lament the fact that they might  have kept in contact more  easily in the modern era of social media  but they part on great terms  kumako isn't the only ex that daniel  gets to finally say goodbye to  either ali also returns to the picture  after she and johnny reconnect on  facebook though johnny has finally begun  a romantic relationship with miguel's  mom carmen  he can't resist the chance to catch up  with his high school flame the two spend  a whole day together having fun at lunch  and an arcade and she takes him to a  country club party that daniel  also attends you remember johnny  lawrence  right how can i forget  ali is bemused to find her former flames  fighting just like old times but  correctly calls them out for being more  alike than they'd like to admit she  also accepts daniel's apology for ending  things so abruptly and thanks johnny for  making her feel young again  before wishing him well with carmen the  memory of fighting over ally has always  been a point of contention for daniel  and johnny but now that the two have  gotten a chance to talk things out with  her  they can finally let go of that piece of  their animosity  and the truth is you guys are more alike  than you want to admit  johnny and carmen aren't the only new  lovebirds taking flight this season  it looks like miguel and sam are also  ready to octopi  some space together again too after  training with johnny  miguel is back in fighting shape and  returns to school  sam apologizes to miguel helps raise  money for his treatments and even shows  him around  miyagi dough the site of them together  might make robbie incensed and it even  raises eyebrows with daniel but sam and  miguel share more than just some  smooches  together they hatch a plan to unite  their dojos for the greater good  meanwhile demetri and yasmin have become  unlikely kissing buddies  not that she'd ever admit that in public  of course and something is definitely  brewing between robbie and tori  after robbie is released from juvenile  detention he and tori bond over their  equally crummy upbringings  and their mutual dissatisfaction with  the idea of miguel and sam  getting back together whether these two  will combine their anger to form a  butt-kicking power couple remains to be  seen  but based on the looks they give each  other in the final episodes we wouldn't  be surprised if their relationship  is about to heat up off the mat  at first miguel has trouble convincing  the members of johnny's new eagle fang  dojo to join forces with sam's miyagi  dome members  but once the kobra kais attack them all  at their christmas party the battle  lines are officially drawn  this means former besties turned rivals  mitch and chris  and bert and nathaniel can finally fight  together again  instead of forcing themselves to hate  each other perhaps the most surprising  member to join this new team  is hawk he is initially poised to be  cobra kai's new champion  and takes kris's tough teachings to  heart even breaking dimitri's arm during  an off the mat confrontation  all season long though hawk watches with  disdain as crease recruits most of his  least favorite people to join the dojo  including his former bully kyler and  robbie  who hawke still blames for what happened  to miguel  look i know some of these guys and  they're natural athletes  which is exactly what's been missing in  our dojo hawk participates in the siege  on miyagi doe  but upon seeing his teammates attacking  his former friends  he decides to switch sides and defends  dimitri against having his arm broken  again  he takes dimitri's side at miyagidou for  the first day of dual training with  eagle fang  making it clear that these two are  finally ready to fight side by side  after so much turmoil after the  kobrakai's attack the unsuspecting kids  at miyagidou  johnny decides to confront his former  sensei once and for all  he's surprised to find his son robbie at  the dojo rising to crease his defense  but johnny still engages crease in a  fight that very nearly turns deadly  robbie discourages johnny from using a  sigh on kris  after he gains the upper hand and kris  makes him pay for that moment of mercy  after robbie himself tries to pick a  fight with johnny  johnny accidentally knocks him out  against a locker  and crease nearly chokes johnny to death  however  daniel arrives in the nick of time and  kicks crease off of johnny  after a brief fight daniel uses miyagi's  disabling move to stop crease in his  tracks  kris suggests that instead of this  turning into a death match  they finish the fight by entering their  students in the all valley tournament  they all stood up to save  if cobra kai loses kris promises to  disappear from town for good  while johnny and daniel unite to take  crease down however  crease maintains one last trick up his  sleeve  throughout cobra kai season 3 we finally  learn why crease is so hell-bent on his  strike first and no mercy philosophies  after enduring the death of his mother  and bullying in his workplace  young crease finally fought back when  one of his tormentors hid his girlfriend  betsy who then became chris's girlfriend  he signed up for a tour in vietnam  shortly after  and was recruited for a covert mission  alongside his friends  ponytail and twig tragically the entire  unit was captured  on that mission ponytail was immediately  executed  while the others were made to fight one  another to the death above a pit of  snakes  kris's captain who regularly accused him  of cowardice  was chosen to fight twig and kries  volunteered to take twig's place  the captain nearly defeated kris after  he revealed beth had died in a car  accident  but kris gained the upper hand even as  they were saved by air support  kris kicked the captain into the pit and  declared he'd finally learned his lesson  show no mercy twigg who may not have  seen kris kick the captain  told kris that he owed him a life debt  and would always be there for whatever  crease needed  now it appears kris is finally ready to  collect after crease makes his deal with  johnny and daniel to settle their  disputes at the tournament he makes a  call to an old friend  while holding a photo of himself with  ponytail and  twig check out one of our newest videos  right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite movies  and tv shows are coming soon subscribe  to our youtube channel and hit the bell  so you don't miss a single one
 

